<title>SPAIN: BBV pays second interim dividend 47 ptas gross.</title>
<headline>BBV pays second interim dividend 47 ptas gross.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Bilbao Vizcaya will pay a second interim dividend of 47 pesetas per share, from October 10, a bulletin from the Madrid bourse said.</p>
<p>The 47 peseta gross dividend is unchanged from the previous one, which the bank paid on July 10. The bank pays dividends on a quarterly basis, in July, October and January plus an extra one in April.</p>
<p>In 1995 the quarterly interim dividend was 42 pesetas gross and the April one amounted to 72 pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 341 585 2160</p>
</text>
